Package: libva-v4l2-iris
Architecture: arm64
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, ${shlibs:Depends}, v4l-utils
Description: VA-API backend for the Qualcomm Iris V4L2 stateful decoder and encoder
 A libVA driver that drives the Qualcomm Iris V4L2 stateful decoder and
 encoder, so VA-API clients such as Chromium, Google Chrome and FFmpeg decode
 and encode H.264, HEVC, VP9 and AV1 in hardware instead of falling back to a
 CPU codec.
 .
 The package installs the driver into libva's driver directory together with
 a read-only device report and a one-command hardware check. Clients need no
 wrapper and no environment variable: libva resolves the driver through the
 msm_drv_video.so alias. Diagnostic commands refuse to guess a /dev/video
 number, because the decoder node moves between boots on this device; they
 resolve it by its iris_driver QUERYCAP name, which is why v4l-utils is a
 hard dependency.
 .
 The VA video processor (scale, crop, rotation, mirroring, HDR tone mapping,
 compositing) is compiled in when the Vulkan loader and headers are present
 and stays behind the V4L2_VA_VPP opt-in at runtime.
